{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "letter-to-orson-hyde-7-april-1834", "page": "3", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_082_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "82", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-orson-hyde-7-april-1834/1"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_083_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "83", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-orson-hyde-7-april-1834/2"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_084_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "84", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-orson-hyde-7-april-1834/3"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-orson-hyde-7-april-1834", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD4", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to Orson Hyde, 7 April 1834", "editorialPageNumber": "84", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/31149/31149-0003.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> ride her very fast in a day and be very careful that I may not loose her and perhaps I may dispose of her to good advantage for the benefit of Zion—<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8570989485571467172\"><a href=\"#8570989485571467172\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans16\"><span id=\"documenttrans16\">16</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Financial records of the <a href=\"/place/missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Missouri</a> expedition note that in April, JS purchased “one Cream Colored Horse” from <a href=\"/person/isaac-mcwithy\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Isaac McWithy</a> for eighty-five dollars. JS had attended a <a href=\"/topic/conference\" class=\"referenceInPop\">conference</a> with McWithy on 17 March in <a href=\"/place/avon-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Avon</a>, New York, and had stayed with him the night of 19–20 March. Perhaps JS arranged for the purchase of a horse from McWithy at that time and instructed <a href=\"/person/orson-hyde\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Hyde</a> to bring the horse to <a href=\"/place/kirtland-township-ohio\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Kirtland</a> when he came. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/account-with-the-camp-of-israel-circa-11-29-august-1834\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/account-with-the-camp-of-israel-circa-11-29-august-1834\" poptitle=\"Account with the Camp of Israel, circa\n11–29 August 1834\">Account with the Camp of Israel, ca. 11–29 Aug. 1834</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/minutes-17-march-1834\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/minutes-17-march-1834\" poptitle=\"Minutes, 17 March\n1834\">Minutes, 17 Mar. 1834</a>; JS, Journal, <a href=\"/paper-summary/journal-1832-1834/64\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/journal-1832-1834\" poptitle=\"19 March 1834 • Wednesday\">19 Mar. 1834</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> I am yours by every sacred and holy tie that can bind up souls</div> <div class=\"right wasptag\">Joseph Smith Jr</div> <div class=\"right wasptag\"> <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13031747412657841970\"><a href=\"#13031747412657841970\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per63\" person=\"per63\" title=\"Frederick Granger Williams\">F G Williams</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Williams, Frederick Granger\"><p>28 Oct. 1787–10 Oct. 1842. Ship’s pilot, teacher, physician, justice of the peace. Born at Suffield, Hartford Co., Connecticut. Son of William Wheeler Williams and Ruth Granger. Moved to Newburg, Cuyahoga Co., Ohio, 1799. Practiced Thomsonian botanical system...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/frederick-granger-williams\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10678681806989228704\"><a href=\"#10678681806989228704\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per47\" person=\"per47\" title=\"Oliver Cowdery\">Oliver Cowdery</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Cowdery, Oliver\"><p>3 Oct. 1806–3 Mar. 1850. Clerk, teacher, justice of the peace, lawyer, newspaper editor. Born at Wells, Rutland Co., Vermont. Son of William Cowdery and Rebecca Fuller. Raised Congregationalist. Moved to western New York and clerked at a store, ca. 1825–1828...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside> [p. 84]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> [ride?] her very fast in a day and be very car[e]ful <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that I may not loose her and perhaps I may <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>dispose of her to good advantage for the bene<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>fit of Zion—<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7628363682993911381\"><a href=\"#7628363682993911381\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans16\"><span id=\"documenttrans16\">16</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Financial records of the <a href=\"/place/missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Missouri</a> expedition note that in April, JS purchased “one Cream Colored Horse” from <a href=\"/person/isaac-mcwithy\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Isaac McWithy</a> for eighty-five dollars. JS had attended a <a href=\"/topic/conference\" class=\"referenceInPop\">conference</a> with McWithy on 17 March in <a href=\"/place/avon-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Avon</a>, New York, and had stayed with him the night of 19–20 March. Perhaps JS arranged for the purchase of a horse from McWithy at that time and instructed <a href=\"/person/orson-hyde\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Hyde</a> to bring the horse to <a href=\"/place/kirtland-township-ohio\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Kirtland</a> when he came. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/account-with-the-camp-of-israel-circa-11-29-august-1834\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/account-with-the-camp-of-israel-circa-11-29-august-1834\" poptitle=\"Account with the Camp of Israel, circa\n11–29 August 1834\">Account with the Camp of Israel, ca. 11–29 Aug. 1834</a>; <a href=\"/paper-summary/minutes-17-march-1834\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/minutes-17-march-1834\" poptitle=\"Minutes, 17 March\n1834\">Minutes, 17 Mar. 1834</a>; JS, Journal, <a href=\"/paper-summary/journal-1832-1834/64\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/journal-1832-1834\" poptitle=\"19 March 1834 • Wednesday\">19 Mar. 1834</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> I am yours by every sacred <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and holy tie that can bind up souls</div> <div class=\"right wasptag\">Joseph Smith Jr</div> <div class=\"right wasptag\"> <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13469793486837871669\"><a href=\"#13469793486837871669\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per63\" person=\"per63\" title=\"Frederick Granger Williams\">F G Williams</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Williams, Frederick Granger\"><p>28 Oct. 1787–10 Oct. 1842. Ship’s pilot, teacher, physician, justice of the peace. Born at Suffield, Hartford Co., Connecticut. Son of William Wheeler Williams and Ruth Granger. Moved to Newburg, Cuyahoga Co., Ohio, 1799. Practiced Thomsonian botanical system...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/frederick-granger-williams\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10462401288851898017\"><a href=\"#10462401288851898017\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per47\" person=\"per47\" title=\"Oliver Cowdery\">Oliver Cowde[r]y</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Cowdery, Oliver\"><p>3 Oct. 1806–3 Mar. 1850. Clerk, teacher, justice of the peace, lawyer, newspaper editor. Born at Wells, Rutland Co., Vermont. Son of William Cowdery and Rebecca Fuller. Raised Congregationalist. Moved to western New York and clerked at a store, ca. 1825–1828...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside> [p. 84]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Letter to Orson Hyde, 7 April 1834", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-orson-hyde-7-april-1834/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Letterbook 1", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letterbook-1/94", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": " History, 1838–1856, volume A-1 [23 December 1805–30 August 1834]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-a-1-23-december-1805-30-august-1834/456", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "“History of Joseph Smith”", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-of-joseph-smith/239", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_084_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_084_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_084.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_084_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_084.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "1605", "requestedPageNumber": "3", "numberOfPages": "3", "editorialTitle": "Letter to Orson Hyde, 7 April 1834", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Letter to Orson Hyde, 7 April 1834", "date": "April 7, 1834", "handwriting": "Handwriting of Frederick G. Williams",